### Finding 2 — Middleware tenant alias drift
**Status**: ✅ **CONFIRMED**

[tenant.go:83-85](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/middleware/tenant.go#L83-L85) sets THREE keys:
```go
c.Set("tenant_id", tenantID)
c.Set("tenantID", tenantID)
c.Set("tenantId", tenantID)
```

[tenant.go:99](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/middleware/tenant.go#L99) [GetTenantID()](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/middleware/tenant.go#96-108) iterates all three keys. This means the contract drift is never broken — any handler can use any variant.

**Additionally discovered**: Handlers use inconsistent retrieval:
- `middleware.GetTenantID(c)` — correct canonical path
- `c.GetString("tenantID")` — direct camelCase access (found in `ads_handler.go:48`, `price_handler.go:24`, `stock_handler.go:25`, `image_handler.go:45`, `inventory/price_handler.go:39`)

**Severity**: Medium — this perpetuates inconsistency across the codebase.

