## Part 2: Additional Bugs Discovered During Analysis

### Bug A — [CheckAllConnections](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/handlers/platform_auth_handler.go#150-237) response uses camelCase `checkedAt`
[platform_auth_handler.go:234](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/handlers/platform_auth_handler.go#L234):
```go
"checkedAt": now,
```
Should be `"checked_at"` per canonical snake_case.

### Bug B — [image_handler.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/handlers/image_handler.go) uses `c.GetString("tenantID")` directly
[image_handler.go:45, 148, 212, 248](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/handlers/image_handler.go): All four handler methods use `c.GetString("tenantID")` instead of `middleware.GetTenantID(c)`, bypassing the canonical accessor.

### Bug C — [GetProductModelsByID](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/handlers/shopee/db_products.go#100-137) ignores Find error
[shopee/db_products.go:119](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/handlers/shopee/db_products.go#L119): This is more serious than Finding 24 because it joins data from this unvalidated query.

### Bug D — Batch price sync history hardcodes `"success"` status
[inventory/price_handler.go:236](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/handlers/inventory/price_handler.go#L236):
```go
Status: "success", // Batch handler returns success if no global error
```
Even if all individual items failed, the batch history entry is `"success"`.

### Bug E — `settings_service.go:111` ignores json.Unmarshal error
```go
json.Unmarshal([]byte(settings.InventorySelectedColumns), &selectedColumns)
```
Error discarded. If the stored JSON is corrupted, `selectedColumns` remains nil/empty.

### Bug F — `log.Printf` at 50+ locations across backend
Far more widespread than the 3 files mentioned in Finding 29. Full list: [clone_inventory.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/services/products/clone_inventory.go), [clone_helpers.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/services/products/clone_helpers.go), [image_cleanup_handler.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/services/jobs/image_cleanup_handler.go), [multi_tenant_executor.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/services/jobs/multi_tenant_executor.go), [executor.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/services/jobs/executor.go), [escrow_sync_handler.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/services/jobs/escrow_sync_handler.go), `autofunction/executor.go`, `autofunction/scheduler.go`, `autofunction/multi_tenant_scheduler.go`, [shopee_escrow_repopulate.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/services/analytics/shopee_escrow_repopulate.go), [price_orchestrator.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/services/inventory/price_orchestrator.go), [stock_orchestrator.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/services/inventory/stock_orchestrator.go), [image_handler.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/handlers/image_handler.go), [global_config.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/config/global_config.go), [auth_handler.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/handlers/auth_handler.go).

### Bug G — `ptrString` function duplicated
[inventory/price_handler.go](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/handlers/inventory/price_handler.go) and [inventory/stock_handler.go:125](file:///d:/Project/omni/backend/internal/handlers/inventory/stock_handler.go#L125) both define their own `ptrString` helper. Should be in a shared utility.

